    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d651">

                <pb facs="0627" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/6381</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-13T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your cipher telegrams of August 9, 8 p.m., and August 11, 11 p.m. The Department
                    believes that the character of China’s participation <pb facs="0628" n="456"
                        xml:id="pg456"/> in the war should be decided by her after consultation with
                    all the Allied Governments. Consult your Allied colleagues informally and report
                    their views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
